# Configuration for MagShockZ2D — the 2D (x-y) reduction of the MagShockZ3D
# laser-driven magnetized shock problem, built for the laser ray-trace /
# deposition convergence scan (see README.md).
#
# Layered in y, which is the beam-propagation direction, exactly as the 3D problem:
#
#     y > sim_PlasmaThickiness                          vac   (chamber wall)
#     sim_AblatorThickiness < y < sim_PlasmaThickiness  cham  (Al foam ambient)
#     0 < y < sim_AblatorThickiness                     targ  (Si target)
#     y < 0                                             vac   (backing)
#
# The applied field is uniform and OUT OF PLANE (magz): the MagShockZ shock is
# perpendicular, so no in-plane field lines exist and a 2D x-y plane carries the
# whole field as a single cell-centered component.  Parameter names deliberately
# match the 3D deck (including its spelling of "Thickiness") so a 3D flash.par
# transfers its values here verbatim rather than being re-typed.
#
# Setup line:
#
#   ./setup -auto MagShockZ2D -2d -nxb=16 -nyb=16 +cartesian +hdf5typeio \
#           species=cham,targ,vac +mtmmmt +laser +usm3t +mgd mgd_meshgroups=1 \
#           -maxblocks=500 -site perlmutter.nersc.gov

REQUIRES Driver
REQUIRES physics/Hydro
REQUIRES physics/Diffuse/DiffuseFluxBased
REQUIRES physics/Eos/EosMain/Tabulated

USESETUPVARS ThreeT

IF ThreeT
   REQUESTS physics/Diffuse/DiffuseMain/Unsplit
   REQUESTS physics/sourceTerms/Heatexchange/HeatexchangeMain/Spitzer
   REQUESTS physics/materialProperties/Conductivity/ConductivityMain/JiHeld
   REQUIRES physics/materialProperties/MagneticResistivity/MagneticResistivityMain
   REQUESTS physics/materialProperties/MagneticResistivity/MagneticResistivityMain/SpitzerHighZ
ENDIF

##########################
#                        #
#   GEOMETRY PARAMETERS  #
#                        #
##########################

D sim_AblatorThickiness Thickness of the solid target slab, from y = 0 upward [cm]
PARAMETER sim_AblatorThickiness REAL 2000.e-4

D sim_PlasmaThickiness Top of the ambient plasma column; vacuum above it [cm]
PARAMETER sim_PlasmaThickiness  REAL 40000.e-4

##########################
#                        #
#   FIELD PARAMETERS     #
#                        #
##########################

D sim_MagField Uniform out-of-plane field Bz, in FLASH's unitsystem=none units
D & (Gauss / sqrt(4 pi)), so 7 T = 70 kG is 1.9747e4 here
PARAMETER sim_MagField REAL 1.9747e+04

##########################
#                        #
#   MATERIAL PARAMETERS  #
#                        #
##########################

# Target: Si slab.
D sim_rhoTarg Initial target density
PARAMETER sim_rhoTarg   REAL 2.33
D sim_teleTarg Initial target electron temperature
PARAMETER sim_teleTarg  REAL 500.02911375
D sim_tionTarg Initial target ion temperature
PARAMETER sim_tionTarg  REAL 500.02911375
D sim_tradTarg Initial target radiation temperature
PARAMETER sim_tradTarg  REAL 500.002911375
D sim_eosTarg target EOS type
PARAMETER sim_eosTarg   STRING "eos_tab" ["eos_tab","eos_gam"]

# Ambient: Al foam.  This is the material whose laser heating the scan is about.
D sim_rhoCham Initial chamber density
PARAMETER sim_rhoCham   REAL 0.0000373
D sim_teleCham Initial chamber electron temperature
PARAMETER sim_teleCham  REAL 114060.
D sim_tionCham Initial chamber ion temperature
PARAMETER sim_tionCham  REAL 114060.
D sim_tradCham Initial chamber radiation temperature
PARAMETER sim_tradCham  REAL 114060.
D sim_eosCham chamber EOS type
PARAMETER sim_eosCham   STRING "eos_tab" ["eos_tab","eos_gam"]

# Backing / wall: stainless steel.
D sim_rhoVac Initial backing density
PARAMETER sim_rhoVac   REAL 7.75
D sim_teleVac Initial backing electron temperature
PARAMETER sim_teleVac  REAL 100.02911375
D sim_tionVac Initial backing ion temperature
PARAMETER sim_tionVac  REAL 100.02911375
D sim_tradVac Initial backing radiation temperature
PARAMETER sim_tradVac  REAL 100.0002911375
D sim_eosVac backing EOS type
PARAMETER sim_eosVac   STRING "eos_tab" ["eos_tab","eos_gam"]

##########################
#                        #
#   LASER DIAGNOSTICS    #
#                        #
##########################

D lase_variable Irradiance deposited by the EnergyDeposition unit, cf. ed_irradVarName
VARIABLE lase TYPE: PER_VOLUME
